# how does [[quantum mechanics|quantum mechanics]] differ from classical physics?
- energy, [[momentum|momentum]], angular momentum  etc. are restricted to discrete values
- objects have characteristics of both particles and waves ([[wave-particle duality|wave-particle duality]])
- there are limits to how accurately the value of a physical quantity can be predicted prior to its [[measurement|measurement]] given a complete set of initial conditions ([[uncertainty principle|uncertainty principle]])
